instructions:
Find three examples of Rätoromanisch words or phrases in Graubünden.
The words can be found on:
signs;
public information boards;
place names;
advertisements;
official displays;
other public sources.
For each word:
Take a photo showing the Rätoromanisch word.
Guess what the word means.
Verify the meaning using an available source (for example, translation information, a sign explanation, or another reliable source).
The team must correctly identify the meaning of all three words.  If you guess any of the words wrong, you must find a new one for it to count

Create a postcard-style photo from three photos of iconic areas within Canton Lucerne.
You need to take photos of the following:
1) A lake;
2) at least one mountain;
3) something created by a human
After you take a photo of each of these objects, you must verify that it has a google ratings score of at least 4.5 stars or above.  If it does not, you must find a new object.  You cannot use do research on google beforehand to determine ratings or favourite tourist locations.  Each object must be located at least 1km away from each other.

Find 11 different examples connected to the number 11 in Solothurn.
The examples must show the number 11 either:
written as the number "11";
represented numerically;
Examples may include:
signs;
buildings;
symbols;
objects;
historical references. Each 11 you find must be at located least 11m meters from other 11's.

Travel to the Morgarten battlefield area in Schwyz.
At the location:
Find a historical marker, monument, or information board connected to the Battle of Morgarten.
Take a photo of your team reenacting a scene inspired by the battle.
The photo must clearly show:the historical location;
your team’s reenactment;
a connection to the Battle of Morgarten.

Your team must also explain:
who fought in the battle;
why Morgarten is important in Swiss history.

Take a photo of five different apples in Thurgau. The apples cannot be available for purchase.
The apples must have visibly different characteristics, such as:
different colours;
different sizes;
different varieties;
different appearances.
Arrange the apples photo from lightest to darkest and send them to the opposing team.

Travel to a location in Valais where the Matterhorn is visible.
Complete the challenge by:
Taking a photo showing:
your team;
the Matterhorn;
